{
  "requirement": "Each listed reference identifies a visible file. Follow `next` to retrieve further pages.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject has two obligations. Each listed reference must identify a visible file, and `next` must be followable to get further pages. The reviewed tests cover both.\n\n**Each listed reference identifies a visible file**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[gitignore_is_shared_by_all_operations_with_or_without_a_git_repository]` runs with and without a Git repository.\n  - It asserts that `Sources::list` includes `keep.txt`, `src/nested.txt` and `.visible`.\n  - It asserts that `Sources::list` excludes ignored files, including one that Git tracks, and excludes `skip/` and `.git/` contents.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/fn[listing_continuations_return_complete_paths_from_the_original_listing]` creates an `empty_directory`. It asserts that the paged `list_sources` output equals exactly the expected file references, so the directory is not listed as a file.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[configured_agent_uses_domain_source_tools_in_independent_executions]` runs the real `list_sources` tool against a directory with a `.gitignore`. It asserts that every listed entry has an integer node `id`. It also asserts that only `visible/selected.txt` among the `visible*` paths is registered as read.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[source_tools_forward_arguments_and_present_discovery_and_read_results]` asserts that the tool returns the provider's listed resources as `{\"files\":[resource]}`. It does this with and without a prefix, and it asserts that no dependencies are registered.\n\n**Follow `next` to retrieve further pages**\n- The `listing_continuations...` test lists 2000 files and asserts that the first page has a string `next`. It then loops `get_next_page` until `next` is absent and concatenates the pages. It asserts that the concatenation equals the complete original list, in order and without duplicates.\n- It writes `added.rs` after the first page and asserts that this file is absent from the continuation. That shows later pages come from the original listing.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[source_discovery_and_its_pages_do_not_register_reads]` follows `next` for `list_sources`. It asserts that each page delivery has no dependencies.\n\nI found no plausible violating behavior that these tests would accept.",
  "references": "9baa746316852e77c6f095dcf82bb8f167d024bf5c3acc3e821082f35c552fa4",
